    "***\n",
    "\n",
    "_**DELETE BEFORE PUBLISHING**_\n",
    "\n",
    "## Style guide reference\n",
    "\n",
    "### Headers\n",
    "\n",
    "Use the HTML classes shown throughout the worked example above and defined in the CSS cell:\n",
    "\n",
    "- `usecase-header-bar` for the top header background bar\n",
    "- `usecase-title` for the main title of the usecase\n",
    "- `usecase-authors`, `usecase-date`, `usecase-duration`, `usecase-level`, `usecase-skill` for the metadata fields\n",
    "- `usecase-level-skill` as a flex container for the level and skill layout\n",
    "- `usecase-section-header` for numbered top-level sections (1., 2., 3.)\n",
    "- `usecase-subsection-header` for numbered subsections (1.1., 1.2.)\n",
    "- `usecase-subsubsection-header` for numbered sub-subsections (1.1.1.) — only use this if a subsection genuinely needs breaking down further\n",
    "- `usecase-subsection-blurb` for an italicised note or callout, not counted in the numbering\n",
    "- `usecase-heading-description` directly underneath **every** heading at any level — this is required, not optional\n",
    "- `usecase-key-takeaways` for highlighting important summary takeaways\n",
    "- `usecase-toc-title` for the contents page title\n",
    "- `usecase-contents` for the contents page\n",
    "- `usecase-code-divider` for the block separating template intro from code\n",
    "\n",
    "### Clickable Table of Contents\n",
    "\n",
    "To ensure users can click the Contents list and jump to the relevant section, do the following:\n",
    "\n",
    "1. **Add a unique ID to your section header tag:** `<div id=\"my-section\" class=\"usecase-section-header\"><b>Header Title</b></div>`\n",
    "2. **Wrap your contents list item in an anchor tag pointing to that ID:** `<a href=\"#my-section\">Header Title</a>`\n",
    "\n",
    "## Plot colour schemes\n",
    "1. Use the same colour (Primary Green) or the colour palette below (in order) throughout your notebook, unless there are more than 5 colours in your plot\n",
    "\n",
    "#### 1) If your plots need to show distinct features, use the following colours in order:\n",
    "\n",
    "| Colour | Hex |\n",
    "|-----|-----|\n",
    "|<p style=\"color:#059669;\">Primary Green</p>|#059669|\n",
    "|<p style=\"color:#9333EA;\">Distinct Purple</p>|#9333EA|\n",    
    "|<p style=\"color:#F97316;\">Distinct Orange</p>|#F97316|\n",
    "|<p style=\"color:#2563EB;\">Distinct Blue</p>|#2563EB|\n",
    "|<p style=\"color:#EBE505;\">Distinct Yellow</p>|#EBE505|\n",
    "\n",
    "See the worked example above for exactly how this looks applied to a real plot.\n",
    "\n",
 ]
